\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces System architecture. On core~1, gyroscope readings are corrected for bias, passed through the deadzone and gain, clipped, and sent to the host as BLE HID mouse reports. On core~0, the unit serves the communicator page and pushes telemetry over Wi-Fi, either through a local network or through its own setup access point. The communicator in the host browser handles dwell selection and speech.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
